c Random Instance of Urquhart's Problem for SAT (size=8).
c Like Hole, this problem as been proved to be exponential for resolution.
c N.B. : instance is unsatisfiable by construction.
c
c Come from the paper 'Hard Examples for Resolution'.
c        Source : Laurent Simon, simon@lri.fr. May 1999.
c
c n=8, so there is m^2=64 vertices in each part of the bipartite graph.
c Bases creations :
c   - a '1' charge is 'there must be an even number of negated vars'
c   - edges contains variables from which all subbases are constructed.
c vertex A0 :(charge=1), (edges=[319,158,138,304,25,204])
c vertex A1 :(charge=1), (edges=[212,152,204,171])
